      "writtenOn": "2022-07-28T16:09:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Once we have more than one group in a regex, we prefer to name the groups\n\n^(?P\u003crepo\u003e@[^/]+)?/(?P\u003cpath\u003e[^:]+):(?P\u003ctarget\u003e.+)$\n\nThis is from an aesthetic point of view to make the regex easier to read. It does not change the result of FindStringSubmatch",
